    <h1>Simplify Co. Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-01">1 October 2026</time></p>

    <h2>1. About this policy</h2>
    <p>Simplify Co. ("we", "us", "our") respects your privacy. This policy explains how we collect, use, store and disclose your personal information, including when you register for our events through LinkedIn or our website. We handle personal information in accordance with the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the Australian Privacy Principles.</p>

    <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
    <p>When you register for an event, we may collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name, email address, job title and organisation</li>
      <li>Any other details you choose to provide in the registration form</li>
      <li>Information about your participation, such as attendance and engagement with event content</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may also collect information when you visit our website, contact us or subscribe to our communications.</p>

    <h2>3. How we collect it</h2>
    <p>We collect personal information directly from you, through LinkedIn registration forms, our website, email or conversations. When you register through LinkedIn, LinkedIn passes your registration details to us. LinkedIn's handling of your information is governed by its own privacy policy.</p>

    <h2>4. How we use your information</h2>
    <p>We use your personal information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Register you for the event and send joining instructions, reminders and follow-up materials</li>
      <li>Run and improve our events and understand who is interested in them</li>
      <li>Send you information about our products, services, events and insights that we think will be useful to you</li>
      <li>Respond to your enquiries</li>
      <li>Meet our legal obligations</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Marketing communications</h2>
    <p>By registering for an event, you consent to receive communications from us about our events, products and services. You can opt out at any time by clicking "unsubscribe" in any email or by contacting us at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. We will action opt-out requests promptly.</p>

    <h2>6. Disclosure of your information</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information. We may share it with trusted service providers who help us deliver our events and communications (for example, webinar, email and customer relationship management platforms). These providers may only use your information for the services they perform for us. We may also disclose information where required or authorised by law.</p>

    <h2>7. Overseas disclosure</h2>
    <p>Some of our service providers, including LinkedIn, may store or process information outside Australia. Where this occurs, we take reasonable steps to make sure your information is handled in a way that is consistent with Australian privacy requirements.</p>

    <h2>8. Security and retention</h2>
    <p>We take reasonable steps to protect your personal information from misuse, loss and unauthorised access. We keep it only for as long as we need it for the purposes above or as the law requires, then securely delete or de-identify it.</p>

    <h2>9. Access and correction</h2>
    <p>You can ask to access or correct the personal information we hold about you by contacting us at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. We will respond within a reasonable time.</p>

    <h2>10. Complaints</h2>
    <p>If you believe we have breached your privacy, contact us at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and we will investigate and respond. If you are not satisfied with our response, you can contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC) at <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>.</p>

    <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be available on this page.</p>

